(1120471, 136526, 23913, '<td valign="top">this is an intrusting image but there are several things that bother me about it<br/>1 of which is the eye..it appears to be looking toward the camer which is kinda unnatrual and distracting from the image. the technique is ok (just plan backlighting but done well) however the skin tones ever for shadow or low light are all off. lastly the position of the person, IMO should be more sideways and less 3/4 or maybe it is me but it looks like the photog. is the subject it this, seems as if the person in the image is also holding the camer which would explain the 3/4ish nature to the model.<br/> <br/>my recomendation next time use the timer or a remot, with a custom white bal., and a lower ISO&amp;middel shutter like 1/60<br/> <br/>it might produce more of a siloquette and get the skin to be skin like as well as lighting the gun just fine GL in the challenge fine image great idea, could have better exicution to make it less "rough around the edges"(so to speak).<br/> <br/>5</td>', 'this is an intrusting image but there are several things that bother me about it1 of which is the eye..it appears to be looking toward the camer which is kinda unnatrual and distracting from the image. the technique is ok (just plan backlighting but done well) however the skin tones ever for shadow or low light are all off. lastly the position of the person, IMO should be more sideways and less 3/4 or maybe it is me but it looks like the photog. is the subject it this, seems as if the person in the image is also holding the camer which would explain the 3/4ish nature to the model. my recomendation next time use the timer or a remot, with a custom white bal., and a lower ISO&middel shutter like 1/60 it might produce more of a siloquette and get the skin to be skin like as well as lighting the gun just fine GL in the challenge fine image great idea, could have better exicution to make it less "rough around the edges"(so to speak). 5', '2005-01-19 22:36:42.000000', NULL, 1),
