(1121485, 137748, 27845, '<td valign="top">Interesting technique. I just wish the picture was just as interesting. 4.</td>', 'Interesting technique. I just wish the picture was just as interesting. 4.', '2005-01-20 13:48:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121491, 137815, 22537, '<td valign="top">The colors are great and the path meanders nicely through the photo and makes the shot quite pleaseing.  It appears slightly oversharpened and the void in the very top right hand corner might have been cropped out.  Good luck.</td>', 'The colors are great and the path meanders nicely through the photo and makes the shot quite pleaseing.  It appears slightly oversharpened and the void in the very top right hand corner might have been cropped out.  Good luck.', '2005-01-20 13:50:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121496, 137736, 22537, '<td valign="top">This has a very fresh appeal to it. The colors are subtle and the shot is well balanced.  The bubbles are crisp and not too oversharpened. This is a fun shot.  Good luck.</td>', 'This has a very fresh appeal to it. The colors are subtle and the shot is well balanced.  The bubbles are crisp and not too oversharpened. This is a fun shot.  Good luck.', '2005-01-20 13:52:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121500, 137706, 22537, '<td valign="top">A good crisp shot and the angle makes me switch from seeing it as a building to a series of paths.  This may be the effect you are looking for and you certainly have accomplished.  Good luck.</td>', 'A good crisp shot and the angle makes me switch from seeing it as a building to a series of paths.  This may be the effect you are looking for and you certainly have accomplished.  Good luck.', '2005-01-20 13:53:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121508, 137430, 22537, '<td valign="top">I have no idea what this is, hence the name?  It is a pleasing photo both in colors and effect.  Had you lost some of the dark area above and below making an elongated image it may have added some more impact.  Overall, a great shot.  Good luck.</td>', 'I have no idea what this is, hence the name?  It is a pleasing photo both in colors and effect.  Had you lost some of the dark area above and below making an elongated image it may have added some more impact.  Overall, a great shot.  Good luck.', '2005-01-20 13:56:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121520, 137242, 22537, '<td valign="top">I suspect that this an onion.  Either way, The contrast is terrific and the composition is excellent. I really like this shot.  Good luck.</td>', 'I suspect that this an onion.  Either way, The contrast is terrific and the composition is excellent. I really like this shot.  Good luck.', '2005-01-20 14:00:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121530, 137815, 31214, '<td valign="top">Love the peaceful feeling this photo emits.  Great job.</td>', 'Love the peaceful feeling this photo emits.  Great job.', '2005-01-20 14:08:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121551, 137812, 7778, '<td valign="top">To me, this -at first glance- unassuming abstract holds some interest. Luminosity is, I speculate, rarely an attribute of such organic earth-tones tones. Colours and hues commonly suggestive of a dry opacity, of rustic materials or objects are wrought with light here, and this over a respectable range extending from shadows to highlights.<br/> <br/>The blurring, although far from obscure, is significant enough as to leave no ''easy'' anchor for eyes accustomed to pictures with selective focal points or -plains. Instead, the image, appears to ''flow'' from a moderately dark to white, which, effectively, provokes a sense of depth.<br/> <br/>The ''white'' (within the curtain [?]) has no texture, no details. It, really, conveys no information other than the lone suggestion of a light source (the sun?). The extensive darker area (from just beneath the curtain''s edge to the bottom and right margins of the image) is far more telling: all manner of shapes, twirls and vortices dance in this expanse, leaving little doubt as to what is at play here, but enough not to give away anything that could impair a sense of mystery and visual delight.<br/> <br/>While the composition may have been arbitrary (the manner of this photo, I believe, allows for it), remains balanced and ''golden'' :-) with light and dark in relative proportion and with the dark weighing in to the right.<br/> <br/>I have two reservations: a) I cannot see a purpose in the two intersecting lines  and suspect a redundancy introduced by ambiguity (?), and b) the title. While I will not contribute any negative criticism of the given title per se, I also feel unconvinced that it accomplishes what it could with an image which appears to demand more than a name.<br/> <br/>I find this photograph exhilarating, sensual and a very real joy to explore.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-01-26 00:32:28.</i></td>', 'To me, this -at first glance- unassuming abstract holds some interest. Luminosity is, I speculate, rarely an attribute of such organic earth-tones tones. Colours and hues commonly suggestive of a dry opacity, of rustic materials or objects are wrought with light here, and this over a respectable range extending from shadows to highlights. The blurring, although far from obscure, is significant enough as to leave no ''easy'' anchor for eyes accustomed to pictures with selective focal points or -plains. Instead, the image, appears to ''flow'' from a moderately dark to white, which, effectively, provokes a sense of depth. The ''white'' (within the curtain [?]) has no texture, no details. It, really, conveys no information other than the lone suggestion of a light source (the sun?). The extensive darker area (from just beneath the curtain''s edge to the bottom and right margins of the image) is far more telling: all manner of shapes, twirls and vortices dance in this expanse, leaving little doubt as to what is at play here, but enough not to give away anything that could impair a sense of mystery and visual delight. While the composition may have been arbitrary (the manner of this photo, I believe, allows for it), remains balanced and ''golden'' :-) with light and dark in relative proportion and with the dark weighing in to the right. I have two reservations: a) I cannot see a purpose in the two intersecting lines  and suspect a redundancy introduced by ambiguity (?), and b) the title. While I will not contribute any negative criticism of the given title per se, I also feel unconvinced that it accomplishes what it could with an image which appears to demand more than a name. I find this photograph exhilarating, sensual and a very real joy to explore.', '2005-01-20 14:17:56.000000', '2005-01-26 00:32:28.000000', 1),
(1121562, 137322, 7778, '<td valign="top">The sense of flying is perfectly captured here. If Brueghel were alive, I''m sure he would see this scene similarly.<br/> <br/>I ask myself, if this shot would have benefitted from a moderate increase in contrast. On the other hand, I appreciate the restraint exercised in terms of saturation. Both manner (the tilt) and composition (accomodating the tilt) strike me highly effective.</td>', 'The sense of flying is perfectly captured here. If Brueghel were alive, I''m sure he would see this scene similarly. I ask myself, if this shot would have benefitted from a moderate increase in contrast. On the other hand, I appreciate the restraint exercised in terms of saturation. Both manner (the tilt) and composition (accomodating the tilt) strike me highly effective.', '2005-01-20 14:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121566, 136751, 7778, '<td valign="top">I was hungry for something out of the ordinary. Here it is. :-)</td>', 'I was hungry for something out of the ordinary. Here it is. :-)', '2005-01-20 14:25:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121568, 136230, 18868, '<td valign="top">I trust that you will share your technique -- how much of this image was capture, how much was post-editing?  I really like the feel and color.</td>', 'I trust that you will share your technique -- how much of this image was capture, how much was post-editing?  I really like the feel and color.', '2005-01-20 14:26:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121590, 137790, 31637, '<td valign="top">thats creative...fantastic portrait...I''d buy this photo.</td>', 'thats creative...fantastic portrait...I''d buy this photo.', '2005-01-20 14:44:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121591, 137394, 31637, '<td valign="top">not blended right...the sky just doesnt look right</td>', 'not blended right...the sky just doesnt look right', '2005-01-20 14:45:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121594, 137723, 31637, '<td valign="top">nice...but groundbreaking?</td>', 'nice...but groundbreaking?', '2005-01-20 14:46:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121629, 137447, 31036, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot!</td>', 'Excellent shot!', '2005-01-20 15:12:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121634, 136954, 31036, '<td valign="top">Beautiful background!</td>', 'Beautiful background!', '2005-01-20 15:15:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121651, 137104, 6532, '<td valign="top">Lines are tilted.....distracting</td>', 'Lines are tilted.....distracting', '2005-01-20 15:20:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121652, 136044, 31036, '<td valign="top">This is a really interesting photo. The blue/greys really work for me. Reminds me of Charlie''s Angels with a holgraphic twist. Nice Job!</td>', 'This is a really interesting photo. The blue/greys really work for me. Reminds me of Charlie''s Angels with a holgraphic twist. Nice Job!', '2005-01-20 15:21:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121657, 137800, 6532, '<td valign="top">THis would have been more appealing to if the hand was not in the corner.</td>', 'THis would have been more appealing to if the hand was not in the corner.', '2005-01-20 15:22:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121674, 137473, 17507, '<td valign="top">Returning to comment, bumping from an 8 to a 9.<br/> <br/>I''m beginning to understand why stellar images like this so often will get a smattering of 1''s and 2''s - my submission is hovering around a 6.5, and the petulant child in me wants to give this a 1 just so my picture has a slightly better chance of taking a ribbon :P If this one doesn''t place, I will be quite surprised.<br/> <br/>In another challenge, I might have given this a 10. The colors are glorious, as is the lighting, and the composition is definitely unusual. What prevents me from giving this the highest mark is that despite its evident creativity, it doesn''t make me say "How the heck did he do that?" or "I never would have thought of that." The technique is clear just from looking at the image, which can be a good thing, but I think a bit of mystery would have been of benefit in this case.<br/> <br/>Nonetheless, this is a great picture, and I hope to see it featured on the front page on the 26th.</td>', 'Returning to comment, bumping from an 8 to a 9. I''m beginning to understand why stellar images like this so often will get a smattering of 1''s and 2''s - my submission is hovering around a 6.5, and the petulant child in me wants to give this a 1 just so my picture has a slightly better chance of taking a ribbon :P If this one doesn''t place, I will be quite surprised. In another challenge, I might have given this a 10. The colors are glorious, as is the lighting, and the composition is definitely unusual. What prevents me from giving this the highest mark is that despite its evident creativity, it doesn''t make me say "How the heck did he do that?" or "I never would have thought of that." The technique is clear just from looking at the image, which can be a good thing, but I think a bit of mystery would have been of benefit in this case. Nonetheless, this is a great picture, and I hope to see it featured on the front page on the 26th.', '2005-01-20 15:30:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121677, 135755, 17507, '<td valign="top">Returning to comment. This is definitely a "gotcha" picture: I have no idea what this is. My best guess is a single hair or a filament or wire of some kind, but with this degree of abstraction, it''s pretty much impossible to be sure. I like the minimalism a lot.<br/> <br/>I''m giving this an 8, and I would have given it a 9 if the long yellow line on the left were just a bit closer to the center. It''s hovering around the 1/4 mark rather than the generally preferable 1/3. Still, I think this is a great picture, and I look forward to seeing how you did it. <br/> <br/>I''m afraid that this image may be scored substantially lower than it deserves, being possibly too far "out there" for most voters'' tastes. But you never know- and good luck in the final standings!</td>', 'Returning to comment. This is definitely a "gotcha" picture: I have no idea what this is. My best guess is a single hair or a filament or wire of some kind, but with this degree of abstraction, it''s pretty much impossible to be sure. I like the minimalism a lot. I''m giving this an 8, and I would have given it a 9 if the long yellow line on the left were just a bit closer to the center. It''s hovering around the 1/4 mark rather than the generally preferable 1/3. Still, I think this is a great picture, and I look forward to seeing how you did it.  I''m afraid that this image may be scored substantially lower than it deserves, being possibly too far "out there" for most voters'' tastes. But you never know- and good luck in the final standings!', '2005-01-20 15:33:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121682, 137423, 17507, '<td valign="top">The most striking thing about this picture is, as I''m sure you intended, the sort of impressionistic patches of light at the top center. Looks like light being refracted through the vase you mention in the title. I''ve often taken pictures of such refractions by themselves, but never had the creative presence of mind to integrate that into a more complex composition. Bravo for good work.</td>', 'The most striking thing about this picture is, as I''m sure you intended, the sort of impressionistic patches of light at the top center. Looks like light being refracted through the vase you mention in the title. I''ve often taken pictures of such refractions by themselves, but never had the creative presence of mind to integrate that into a more complex composition. Bravo for good work.', '2005-01-20 15:35:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121687, 137691, 17507, '<td valign="top">I don''t know much about infrared photography, but this looks like an example of it. I guess deciduous trees show up white, while coniferous trees show up black? Very striking almost monochromatic palette. The minimalist composition is compelling while the veil of fog with the texture of the foliage keeps it from being stark. Bumping from 8 to 9.</td>', 'I don''t know much about infrared photography, but this looks like an example of it. I guess deciduous trees show up white, while coniferous trees show up black? Very striking almost monochromatic palette. The minimalist composition is compelling while the veil of fog with the texture of the foliage keeps it from being stark. Bumping from 8 to 9.', '2005-01-20 15:37:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121785, 137790, 11270, '<td valign="top">nice shot</td>', 'nice shot', '2005-01-20 16:33:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1121809, 136288, 11270, '<td valign="top">well done....9</td>', 'well done....9', '2005-01-20 16:44:01.000000', NULL, 1),
