(1130058, 137756, 22734, '<td valign="top">Okay, this is nice but it could be improved to be more competitative. Consider, the eye has liquid colors and it has more white. The skin is like a 5th zone. The white is about 8-9 zone. We then give the 5th zone top billing. That is allow 2/3 of the exposure on the closed eye lids and the lesser fraction to the open eye. Depending on light even lesser time may be required for the open eye. Outside of this, you have the technique. Just think that 8 to 10 zones instantly record and can erase any lower zone values. But hey, regardless of my advise, you did a very nice job. Bumping up from 5 to 6.</td>', 'Okay, this is nice but it could be improved to be more competitative. Consider, the eye has liquid colors and it has more white. The skin is like a 5th zone. The white is about 8-9 zone. We then give the 5th zone top billing. That is allow 2/3 of the exposure on the closed eye lids and the lesser fraction to the open eye. Depending on light even lesser time may be required for the open eye. Outside of this, you have the technique. Just think that 8 to 10 zones instantly record and can erase any lower zone values. But hey, regardless of my advise, you did a very nice job. Bumping up from 5 to 6.', '2005-01-24 22:40:20.000000', NULL, 1),
