(1131828, 137133, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice light and good abstract quality.  I''d like to have seen this bigger though.  Also, you might consider cropping the right some--the effect is lost in the right 1/6 of the image.  Bumping up!</td>', 'Nice light and good abstract quality.  I''d like to have seen this bigger though.  Also, you might consider cropping the right some--the effect is lost in the right 1/6 of the image.  Bumping up!', '2005-01-25 21:27:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131829, 137750, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice surreal look to it; seems like it could use some more contrast.  Bumping up.</td>', 'Nice surreal look to it; seems like it could use some more contrast.  Bumping up.', '2005-01-25 21:28:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131830, 137708, 12253, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors and somewhat abstract as presented.  Nice work--bumping up!</td>', 'Beautiful colors and somewhat abstract as presented.  Nice work--bumping up!', '2005-01-25 21:29:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131831, 137447, 12253, '<td valign="top">Neat trick and a good jab at the past!  Bumping up!</td>', 'Neat trick and a good jab at the past!  Bumping up!', '2005-01-25 21:30:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131832, 137791, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.   I think it would work better if the flowers themselves were sharp as a contrast to the background.</td>', 'Nice idea.   I think it would work better if the flowers themselves were sharp as a contrast to the background.', '2005-01-25 21:32:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131833, 137820, 22734, '<td valign="top">A very cool effect proving the high caliber of talent that resides in DPC. Amazing.<br/> <br/>What makes it amazing is that here a special effect has been raised to a mascot of Americana. Oftentimes we start to follow an idea and we force things into place. Sometimes the results are a mish-mash. This, however, is that supreme exception where the spirit of creation takes the drivers seat. Let us examine the image.<br/> <br/>First is  probably a 4x8 board with a cutout. A mosrt appropiate background to confound the viewer. The simple frame and last but not least, the model. I mean, look at this kid in baseball gear. Look at the expression, the healthy look, the gaps between the teeth. Sweet enough? Now, look at the wall paper in relationship to the color  stitching of the baseball and look at how the baseball is not at all sharp but just the right fuzziness to aid the effect. Now study the angle and the passive position of the right hand as opposed to the active left. Well, here is a special effect that is surpassed by the message it delivers. A truly impressive and an unforgettable image.</td>', 'A very cool effect proving the high caliber of talent that resides in DPC. Amazing. What makes it amazing is that here a special effect has been raised to a mascot of Americana. Oftentimes we start to follow an idea and we force things into place. Sometimes the results are a mish-mash. This, however, is that supreme exception where the spirit of creation takes the drivers seat. Let us examine the image. First is  probably a 4x8 board with a cutout. A mosrt appropiate background to confound the viewer. The simple frame and last but not least, the model. I mean, look at this kid in baseball gear. Look at the expression, the healthy look, the gaps between the teeth. Sweet enough? Now, look at the wall paper in relationship to the color  stitching of the baseball and look at how the baseball is not at all sharp but just the right fuzziness to aid the effect. Now study the angle and the passive position of the right hand as opposed to the active left. Well, here is a special effect that is surpassed by the message it delivers. A truly impressive and an unforgettable image.', '2005-01-25 21:32:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131837, 136408, 12253, '<td valign="top">I like the colors here, but I think the technique works better with nonsillouetted subjects--somehow light objects against a dark--or even a light background have the most painterly effect (at least in my experience, and I do this a lot! (too much perhaps)</td>', 'I like the colors here, but I think the technique works better with nonsillouetted subjects--somehow light objects against a dark--or even a light background have the most painterly effect (at least in my experience, and I do this a lot! (too much perhaps)', '2005-01-25 21:34:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1131843, 137595, 22734, '<td valign="top">Dangerous sense of humor, but i will bump you up all the same. lol</td>', 'Dangerous sense of humor, but i will bump you up all the same. lol', '2005-01-25 21:39:45.000000', NULL, 1),
