(1132387, 137820, 18367, '<td valign="top">Another yet absolutely stunning photo by a master.  <br/> <br/>I am ever so glad that I joined DPC, as I have had the good fortune, in a very short period of time, to view some absolutely astounding photography prepared by unbelievably talented individuals.<br/> <br/>Surprising as it may seem Mr. Scalvert,  I did have a good idea as to how the set up for this photograph was done.  I am slowly but surely learning a greal deal from you and others in this realm.<br/> <br/>The photos you grace us with are indeed to be marvelled at, but perhaps (I may sound rather self centered in saying this), what I treasure the most, are the lessons you provide in addition to your artwork.<br/> <br/>Thank you ever so much for being the caring and sharing person that you are!!!<br/> <br/>Ray</td>', 'Another yet absolutely stunning photo by a master.   I am ever so glad that I joined DPC, as I have had the good fortune, in a very short period of time, to view some absolutely astounding photography prepared by unbelievably talented individuals. Surprising as it may seem Mr. Scalvert,  I did have a good idea as to how the set up for this photograph was done.  I am slowly but surely learning a greal deal from you and others in this realm. The photos you grace us with are indeed to be marvelled at, but perhaps (I may sound rather self centered in saying this), what I treasure the most, are the lessons you provide in addition to your artwork. Thank you ever so much for being the caring and sharing person that you are!!! Ray', '2005-01-26 01:13:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1132392, 136037, 255, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i> You crazy :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>for real. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness: You crazy :)   for real. :)', '2005-01-26 01:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1132397, 137822, 18677, '<td valign="top">Sorry there is no description in the Photographer''s Comments section.  The reason is because I submitted this with literally only a few seconds left, and didn''t have enough time to write how I did it.  I''m surprised it actually got in.<br/> <br/>I came up with the idea about 20 minutes before the challenge deadline, and my battery ran out about 10 minutes later.  It''s just a long exposure with a remote flash manually triggered twice, with two different expressions.  I believe it''s unique because the "strobe" effect is only on a small part of the picture, or at least was supposed to be.  It was (obviously) quite difficult to sit still enough with my head in exactly the same place while making a different expression.  I believe I could''ve done a MUCH better job if I had more time and more tries.  This was the best of the 10-15 I was able to do before time ran out.</td>', 'Sorry there is no description in the Photographer''s Comments section.  The reason is because I submitted this with literally only a few seconds left, and didn''t have enough time to write how I did it.  I''m surprised it actually got in. I came up with the idea about 20 minutes before the challenge deadline, and my battery ran out about 10 minutes later.  It''s just a long exposure with a remote flash manually triggered twice, with two different expressions.  I believe it''s unique because the "strobe" effect is only on a small part of the picture, or at least was supposed to be.  It was (obviously) quite difficult to sit still enough with my head in exactly the same place while making a different expression.  I believe I could''ve done a MUCH better job if I had more time and more tries.  This was the best of the 10-15 I was able to do before time ran out.', '2005-01-26 01:20:34.000000', NULL, 0),
