(1132586, 137082, 30214, '<td valign="top">max,<br/>usually motion blur looks nice if there is a sharp subject (here, a fish) in the end of it. It could be achieved either by using a flash in slow sync mode (2nd curtain), or by training a fish to move a bit and then stand still for a couple of seconds. The first is probably impossible because of the glare off the glass wall, the second is pretty hard, too :)</td>', 'max,usually motion blur looks nice if there is a sharp subject (here, a fish) in the end of it. It could be achieved either by using a flash in slow sync mode (2nd curtain), or by training a fish to move a bit and then stand still for a couple of seconds. The first is probably impossible because of the glare off the glass wall, the second is pretty hard, too :)', '2005-01-26 03:40:59.000000', NULL, 0),
